LETTER OF CLAIM UNDER THE PRE-ACTION PROTOCOL FOR HOUSING CONDITIONS CLAIMS (ENGLAND)

We are instructed by the above tenants in connection with a claim for housing disrepair at the above property. Please pass this letter to the landlord and the landlord's insurer immediately.

1. Defects. Our clients report penetrating damp and black mould to the second bedroom (ceiling and external wall), the bathroom ceiling and the window reveals in the living room. These were first reported to you on or around 21 August 2026.

2. Breach. Despite notice, no repair has been carried out. Two appointments (8 and 29 September 2026) were not attended by your contractor. We allege breach of section 11 of the Landlord and Tenant Act 1985 and section 9A of that Act (fitness for human habitation).

3. Personal injury. Our clients' daughter, Ama (aged 6), has asthma which our clients say has been made significantly worse by the mould, including an out-of-hours GP visit on 3 October 2026. A separate letter of claim for personal injury will follow.

4. Disclosure. Under the Protocol, please provide within 20 working days of receipt of this letter: the tenancy agreement; all records of reports, inspections and repair works for the property in the last 6 years; all correspondence with our clients and with contractors about these defects.

5. Expert. We propose a single joint expert surveyor and invite your comments on the enclosed nominee within 20 working days.

6. Response. Please acknowledge this letter and provide a full response, including whether liability is admitted and your proposed schedule of works, within 20 working days of receipt.

Nothing in this letter should delay any repair. Our clients will continue to allow access for works on reasonable notice.

Yours faithfully

